# Build a saved showcase for the light FILTER: ice on one side, green fog on
# the other, a wall torch behind each, and clear torchlight in between.
#
#   tools/headless.sh tools/keys/lightfilter-show.keys 1
#
# It exists because tools/keys/lightshow.keys shows every KIND of source but
# no filtering cell, so it cannot show what src/Light.cpp's transmittance walk
# does. Bead inc-qh0w.
#
# WHAT IT BUILDS, all relative to where the mage arrives:
#   east   a five-cell vertical ICE WALL one step away, with a wall torch
#          three steps away behind it -- torchlight arrives dim and blue
#   west   a wall torch three steps away with nothing in the way -- the same
#          torch, unfiltered, for comparison
#   north  a green Stinking Cloud, an FI_FOG field, so its own colour tints
#          the light that crosses it. North, not west, because the targeting
#          cursor will not cross the west torch either -- trap 3 again, in
#          the spell system rather than the wizard menu.
#
# THREE THINGS THAT BIT THIS SCRIPT, all of them silent:
#
#   1. chargen-mage.keys ends on the Entry Chamber room description, so the
#      first key after arrival is spent dismissing it. Without the SPACE
#      everything after shifts by one and the run ends in an options screen.
#   2. 'w' OPENS the wizard menu; it is not a prefix. After "w y" the menu is
#      already open, so the FIRST placement presses K on its own. Writing
#      "w K" there picks wizard item [w] instead and desynchronises the rest.
#   3. The targeting cursor will not cross a solid cell. Terrain therefore
#      goes down FAR TO NEAR, with each wall torch placed before the ice that
#      would later stand between it and the player.
#
# A mage, not the usual barbarian, because only a caster reaches the fog: the
# cloud is a field cast from the spell system, not a terrain type. The terrain
# called "fog" is a different thing (TF_OBSCURE, no field) and the light map
# does not read it.
#
# Terrain letters from the wizard "Which terrain type?" list:
#   [h] Ice Wall   [p] Wall Torch

@include chargen-mage.keys
@dump:arrival

SPACE
w y

K RIGHT*3 ENTER p
w K RIGHT ENTER h
w K UP RIGHT ENTER h
w K UP*2 RIGHT ENTER h
w K DOWN RIGHT ENTER h
w K DOWN*2 RIGHT ENTER h
w K LEFT*3 ENTER p
@dump:ice-and-torches

w r "Stinking Cloud" ENTER
@dump:spell-learned

m ENTER
UP*4 ENTER
@dump:fog-cast

ESC b
@dump:showcase-saved

@quit
